@doc """
    updateCurrentState(mp, t::Real, strain::Istensor)
    updateCurrentState(mp, t::Real, F::Itensor)

Set the trial state of the material point at time `t`.

# Details
Small strain points take the linearised strain as an [`Istensor`](@ref); finite strain points
take the deformation gradient as a general [`Itensor`](@ref).

This sets the *current* state only. A solver iterating on a step calls this repeatedly, then
either accepts the step with
[`commitCurrentState`](@ref MuesliMaterials.commitCurrentState) or discards it with
[`resetCurrentState`](@ref MuesliMaterials.resetCurrentState).

There is no bang, because the call advances the point's own history rather than filling an
argument.
"""
function updateCurrentState end

