@doc """
    firstPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical!(mp, P::Itensor)

Compute the first Piola-Kirchhoff stress by numerically differentiating the stored energy.

Slower and less accurate than
[`firstPiolaKirchhoffStress!`](@ref MuesliMaterials.firstPiolaKirchhoffStress!), and meant for
checking: if the analytic and numerical stresses disagree, the model is wired up wrongly.
"""
function firstPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical! end

@doc """
    secondPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical!(mp, S::Istensor)

Compute the second Piola-Kirchhoff stress by numerical differentiation of the stored energy.

!!! warning "Broken upstream"
    This does not currently produce a usable result. MUESLI's
    `finiteStrainMP::secondPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical` assigns a general `itensor` into the
    symmetric `istensor` output, which never reaches the symmetric tensor's storage, so `S`
    keeps whatever was already in memory. It is intermittent — sometimes the memory happens to
    look plausible — which makes it worse than a hard failure.

    Use [`firstPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical!`](@ref MuesliMaterials.firstPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical!),
    which is correct, and convert with ``S = F^{-1}P`` if you need the second measure.
"""
function secondPiolaKirchhoffStressNumerical! end

